  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TapEffect: Tap Water Supply, Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale Response Facility - Drinking water</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TapEffect is a piped water system in Cambodia operating in a region near the Thai border, covering an area of approximately 2,300 households. In 2020, they constructed a filtration and storage system in order to provided piped connections to households in the area.Because of COVID-19, many members of the community have had financial hardships and have not been able to cover the initial start-up costs associated with connecting to the water system. Response Facility funding was granted to help these households establish a household water connection despite financial difficulties.</narrative>
  </description>
